// D12 — rundll32 loading a DLL from a non-system drive letter via an export
// Author:  Jenna Frank (Hot Pink Huntress)
// Hunt:    Hunt 22 "Harborlight" — Akira ransomware, Microsoft Sentinel
// ATT&CK:  T1218.011 (System Binary Proxy Execution: Rundll32), T1553.005 (Mark-of-the-Web Bypass)
// Source:  Sysmon EventID 1 (Process Create)
// Status:  Proposed. Replay TP in the hunt window; benign control pending.
//
// EventID 1 where Image ends rundll32.exe and CommandLine matches a non-system drive
// path (D: through Z:) plus a .dll,Export form, or a for loop iterating drive letters
// for a DLL. A D: to Z: path is not by itself proof of a mounted ISO or removable
// media; it can be a fixed or mapped drive.

HarborlightDental_CL
| where EventTime > ago(1d) and EventID == 1 and Image has "rundll32"
| where CommandLine matches regex @"[D-Z]:\\[^,]+\.dll,\w+" or (CommandLine has "for " and CommandLine has "rundll32")
| project EventTime, host, CommandLine

// FP/tuning: FP rate unmeasured; legitimate rundll32 use targets System32 DLLs, but
// software installed on a secondary fixed drive can match. Confirming the drive type
// needs mount or volume telemetry (a CdRom device path in EventID 11, or a mount event).
